A||||7||Predator||Wierd Headlight Problem||||5||
Z||000000||Predator||04-19-2001||07:49 AM||||I have a 1985 Fiero GT. When I turn the headlights on the lights come on, but the motor does nothing if I just push the switch all the way up. If I move the switch up slowly until I hear the motors start up and hold it at that position the headlights come all the way up with no problem. When I flip the switch down they come down fine. I have replaced the switch with a new one, and that did not help. Any ideas?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||04-19-2001||08:03 AM||||Replace the control module under the left front fender in front of the wheel. You have to remove the front of the fender well to get to it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||04-19-2001||08:12 AM||||Thanks, I will check it out. Can I get the Control Module from someplace like NAPA?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-19-2001||07:26 PM||||No you can't.... 85 doesn't have a module there. (Unless someone put 87 or later wiring in it.) it uses several relays and switches in the motors.<P>Just as well.... those modules new are around $200.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Max The Chainsaw||04-19-2001||11:45 PM||||$200!!!!<P>Dang, and to think I've got 2 of em sitting in the garage.... Guess i need to contact E-Bay.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||04-19-2001||11:54 PM||||Dewd just replace your switch, it's a lot cheaper and chances are it will fix the problem. My 84 does the same thing but only on the down position. If I just hit the button the lights go off but not down. If I hold it in the down position then they go down||||reg||4
Z||000006||Predator||04-20-2001||03:14 PM||||Thanks for the responses. I have already replaced the switch and it did not help the problem. The Headlights have three relays. One for each headlight and another that splits the power to them. I will try replacing the main relay.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Spektyr||04-20-2001||03:17 PM||||My understanding is that if you have a problem with one headlight, that side's relay could be bad.  If you have a problem with both headlights it's the main relay.<P>(Assuming it is a relay problem, of course)<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
